{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep My charge.</b> HaShem commands concerning the fences that guard a person so as not to come to stumble in the abomination, and that is His saying <b>and you shall keep My charge</b> — meaning, the charge of the fence. And the reason for ״לְבִלְתִּי עֲשׂוֹת״ and so forth is: even unwittingly. For even though you are not liable for the abomination unwittingly, nevertheless you become defiled through the act of the abomination, and that is His saying <b>and do not defile yourselves through them</b>; and on account of this concern you shall keep My charge." "And His saying <b>I am YHWH your Elohim</b> intends to say that by defiling themselves, even unwittingly, they diminish from the level of the uniqueness of His name, may He be blessed, upon them — for the abomination, in any form it may take, effects a separation between Israel and the Shekhinah, for the Shekhinah rests only upon one who is cleansed of that impurity. And the Holy One, blessed be He, may say to him all that is written for life." "<b>Thus concludes the pericah of Aḥarei.</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:58:42.407413112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}